```
# ============================================================================
# Detection: Cross-Process Memory Write Indicative of Process Injection
# Detection ID: DE-PR-001
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1055 - Process Injection
# Data Source: Sysmon EventCode=8 (CreateRemoteThread), EventCode=10
# Severity: Critical
# ============================================================================

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=8
| search NOT (SourceImage=TargetImage)
| search NOT SourceImage IN ("*\\MsMpEng.exe","*\\SenseIR.exe","*\\CSFalconService.exe")
| stats count min(_time) as first_seen values(TargetImage) as targets by ComputerName, SourceImage, SourceProcessId, StartFunction
| eval first_seen=strftime(first_seen,"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
| sort -count
```

## Detection Logic
CreateRemoteThread events where the source and target images differ indicate one process is writing execution context into another's address space — the core mechanism behind DLL injection, process hollowing, and reflective loading used for privilege escalation and defense evasion.

## False Positive Considerations
EDR/AV self-protection and some legitimate hooking software (accessibility tools, some game anti-cheat) trigger this. Exclude known-good source images by verified hash.

## Tuning Notes
Pair with Sysmon EventCode=25 (ProcessTampering) if using Sysmon 13+ for process-hollowing-specific coverage.
